From c0e6b5d8dbad8d6e1a1fc6cb3e983368d1f0d008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:24:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(api): redact the session token after the router var
 split

`redact_router_session()` looked the session up under the root state's
`router` var. reflex 0.9.12 (reflex-dev/reflex#7068) made `router` a
property with no backing field and split the data into `rx_router_session`,
`rx_router_headers`, `rx_router_page`, `rx_router_url` and
`rx_router_route_id`, so that key is no longer in `state.dict()` or in a
delta: the redaction silently returned the dict untouched and
`POST /_reflex/retrieve_state`, the ndjson event stream, `queue_event` and
the MCP state resources all handed the caller the server-generated
`client_token` -- an identifier the caller never presented, and the one the
websocket path authenticates a session by.

Redact wherever the session lives: the legacy `router` var and the split
`rx_router_session` var, keyed by name from reflex's own constant when it
has one, *and* by the value's `RouterData` / `SessionData` type so a further
rename cannot turn this back into a silent no-op. `_redact_session_value()`
handles the dataclass, the already-serialized dict and reflex's mutable
proxy; `_redact_router_value()` now delegates to it. The MCP single-var read
routes every value through the same function instead of special-casing the
var named `router`, which does not exist on reflex >= 0.9.12.

`client_ip`, the URL, page params and headers stay -- handlers read them.

Verified end to end on the `tickets` demo with reflex 0.9.12a1: both
`retrieve_state` and the event delta carry `rx_router_session` with
`client_token`/`session_id` blanked, where the published 0.9.5 returns the
live token; and on reflex 0.9.11.post1 the legacy `router` var is redacted
exactly as before.

Fixes reflex-dev/reflex#7214

